      "summary": "Dyfed-Powys Police’s account of the night, and why they arrested Dean.",
      "detail": "Dyfed-Powys Police — summary disclosed to Mr D. Pritchard’s solicitor.\n\nSaturday 26 / Sunday 27 October 2024, Hafod Studios, near Rhayader.\nThe deceased, Rhys MORGAN (52), and Dean PRITCHARD (52) argued at the foot of the granary steps. Video recorded by Ms F. HOLT (camera timecode 01:18–01:26) shows PRITCHARD shouting and pushing MORGAN in the chest.\nPRITCHARD first said he went to bed ‘at about one’ and did not see MORGAN after the session. Shown the video, he said they argued and he left MORGAN ‘alive, at about quarter to two’.\n01:41 — MORGAN’s smartwatch detects a hard fall. 01:42 — the watch makes an automated 999 call.\nMrs C. MORGAN, woken by the ambulance service’s call to her as his emergency contact, found her husband at the foot of the steps.\n02:16 — Ambulance on scene. 02:31 — MORGAN pronounced dead.\n\nNo one else was in the yard. Mr E. COLE was on a video call to Los Angeles in the control room, with Mr H. BEVAN, until about 01:55. Mrs MORGAN was on the telephone to her sister in Canada in the farmhouse until about 01:50, then asleep. Ms HOLT and Mr B. LEWIS were asleep. The landing light at the top of the steps was working when tested. All times are taken from the deceased’s watch, the video’s timecode and the witnesses’ phones.\n\nWorking theory: after the argument shown on video, PRITCHARD followed MORGAN up the steps and pushed him.\nPRITCHARD arrested on suspicion of murder, 27 October; released on police bail, 29 October, pending a charging decision by the CPS."
