      "detail": "The ambulance service’s recording of the automated 999 call from Rhys Morgan’s watch, transcribed for the defence. Sunday 27 October 2024. Times are GMT, after the clocks went back.\n\n01:42:05 — Call connects. Automated voice: ‘This is an automated emergency call from a watch. The owner has had a hard fall and is not responding.’ The location follows: Hafod, near Rhayader.\n01:42:30 — Call handler: ‘Ambulance service. Can you hear me? If you can hear me, make a noise.’ No reply. Wind.\n01:42:50 — Footsteps on stone, coming down, quickly. Then, very close: breathing, and a rustle of clothing.\n01:43:10 — A mobile phone rings, very close. The ringtone is an electric guitar riff: the opening bars of ‘Small Hours’. Two rings, then it stops.\n01:43:20 — Footsteps going up stone steps, fast. 01:43:24 — A door closes, above.\n01:45:00 — The call handler rings the emergency contact, Mrs C. Morgan.\n01:46:40 — A woman’s voice, far off and coming closer: ‘Rhys? RHYS!’\n01:46:58 — The same woman, beside the watch, sobbing. Call handler: ‘Hello? Is someone with him?’"
